"description" = "Give your model and dataset folders a home on Hugging Face.\n\nFace Hugger brings local files, remote repositories, and upload activity into one native Mac workspace. Prepare a folder, review the destination, and start when you are ready.\n\nPREPARE WITH CONFIDENCE\nBrowse the local file preview, apply include and exclude filters, and see which previewed paths already exist remotely. File and folder conflicts are flagged before upload. Path checks do not claim that file contents are identical.\n\nKEEP TRANSFERS ORGANIZED\nQueue folders, follow reported preparation, upload or reuse, and commit activity, and stop or resume a transfer when needed. Already-committed files stay on Hugging Face. Saved folder–repository pairings make repeat uploads easier without starting them automatically.\n\nMANAGE THE BASICS\nBrowse model and dataset repositories, choose destination folders, create a repository with explicit public or private visibility, and delete individual remote files after confirmation.\n\nGIVE YOUR DATASET A USEFUL README\nDraft a dataset card from your selected folder’s file names, formats, and sizes. Add its purpose, source, license, and limitations, then review and edit the Markdown. On supported Macs, Apple Intelligence can turn your purpose notes into an overview entirely on device. A template is always available. Compare with an existing local README and save a local copy before choosing to upload. Dataset contents are not sampled for drafting, and nothing is published automatically.\n\nBUILT FOR YOUR MAC\nKeep uploads running when you close the window, return through the menu bar, and receive completion notifications. Optional sleep prevention keeps idle sleep from interrupting an active upload. Quitting the app stops the transfer; resume it when you return.\n\nOn-device drafting requires an Apple Intelligence-compatible Mac with Apple Intelligence enabled and its model ready. All upload and template features work without Apple Intelligence.\n\nA Hugging Face account with permission to write to your chosen repository and an internet connection are required for uploads. Matching remote paths may be replaced. Source folders remain live. If source files change, start a new upload so the updated contents can be reviewed.\n\nFace Hugger is an independent application, not an official Hugging Face product.";
"keywords" = "model,dataset,upload,repository,machine learning,developer,files,transfer,queue,readme";
"promotionalText" = "Upload models and datasets from a native Mac workspace. Draft dataset cards with optional on-device Apple Intelligence, review your files, and keep transfers organized.";
"supportUrl" = "https://bubstack.dev/face-hugger/";
"marketingUrl" = "https://bubstack.dev/face-hugger/";
"whatsNew" = "Face Hugger 1.1 requires macOS 27 and a Mac with Apple silicon. If your Mac has an Intel processor or runs an earlier version of macOS, Face Hugger 1.0 stays available and keeps working.\n\nDataset card drafts are tidier: if the on-device model adds its own License, Citation or Usage section, Face Hugger removes it, so the card keeps only its own sections and your details.";
